      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SURGE (1) stalked the lead from a middle box before hitting the front turning and lifting to score (30.02) at this track in a Mix 6/7 FIN over 525m. Hard to go past. KIWI HANK (3) has a strong winning strike-rate this journey here having won two of four starts. In the money last time at Sandown (29.72) in a Mix 6/7, finishing a 3.5 lengths second. Looks a key chance on best figures. SCARY STORM (7) has some solid form under his belt and proved too strong last time to win by 4 lengths at this track in a handy 29.95 beating Saint Bernardo. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. REV GORDON (8) in the money here last time and looks a top-three prospect again.",
